# Issue #145: a filter's walk reads the flows declared above it, and a
# declaration below joins the view. Y (declared above the filter) is not
# reached through the flow declared below: out. Z (declared below) is
# in by declaration, two flows away from A, out of the walk's reach.
# Expected: A -> B -> Z.
#include tests/non-regression/093-filter-merge-master.dfd

process Y
!>1 A
process Z
A -> Y ay
B -> Z bz
